# v0.198.0-alpha Release Notes

Release: v0.198.0-alpha
Date: 2026-08-14
Tag: v0.198.0-alpha
Status: ALPHA (Defensible Binaries & Sovereign Computation Milestone)

## Highlights

1. Deep Struct Field Level SECRET Taint Tracking
   - Struct fields are individually tracked for secret contamination.
   - Clean fields on sensitive structs can safely be read and passed to sinks.
   - Contaminated fields are strictly refused at build time across all sinks.

2. Complete Package Manager Engine & CLI (ooda/pm)
   - SemVer 2.0.0 parsing, comparison, and caret/tilde range matching.
   - Content-Addressable Storage (CAS) with deterministic lockfile generation.
   - Security guards: capability escalation prevention, SSRF rejection, path traversal blocks.

3. First-Class Object Capabilities & Rights Diminution
   - Pure object capability model with bitmask rights (rwx -> rx).
   - Mathematical diminution preventing privilege escalation on child tokens.
   - Explicit URI prefix bounds checks and expiration timestamps.

4. Host Sandboxing: Linux Landlock & OS Heap Quotas
   - Kernel Landlock filesystem confinement with PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS.
   - OS resource limits (RLIMIT_AS memory quota, RLIMIT_NOFILE descriptor ceiling).

5. Native DNS Resolution under &NetCap
   - std/net/dns.oo providing dns_resolve and dns_resolve_ipv4.
   - Privileged getaddrinfo lookups requiring unforgeable NetCap token nonces.

6. Generative Contract Fuzzer (std/test/fuzz.oo)
   - Boundary explorer and type mutator for integers, strings, and structs.
   - Proves requires and ensures contract enforcement on native Backend-C.

7. Automated Capability Repair (ooda fix)
   - CLI toolchain command detecting E_CAP missing capability errors.
   - Automatically repairs function signatures and call sites with &Cap tokens.

8. Dedicated Long-Term Horizons Board (openOODA/MOONSHOTS.oot)
   - Tracks Automated Binary Transmutation, Autonomous Immune Regeneration,
     Zero-Knowledge Confidential Execution, and Universal Poly-Binaries.

## Verification
- oodac check 100% PASS across all standard library modules and fixtures.
- 100% Rule 1.7 Compliance (all modules <= 256 lines).
- Native Backend-C GCC execution verified with zero regressions.
